{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 2, :comments ["<b>When you come into the land of your dwellings, etc., and you shall make a fire-offering to YHWH.</b> This section is juxtaposed to the section of the spies in order to strengthen the heart of the sons who are mourning, and to comfort them, and to inform them that they will come into the land and offer sacrifices there." "<b>By way of the Midrash.</b> Just as a father exerts himself on behalf of his son in five things — to circumcise him, to teach him Torah, to redeem him from the priest, to teach him a trade, and to marry him to a wife — so did the Holy One, blessed be He, do for Israel. He circumcised them through Joshua, as it is said (Joshua 5): ״עשה לך חרבות צורים.״ Just as a father is obligated to redeem, so the Holy One, blessed be He, redeemed Israel, as it is said (2 Samuel): ״ומי כעמך כישראל גוי אחד בארץ אשר הלכו אלהים לפדות לו לעם.״ To teach him Torah — so the Holy One, blessed be He, taught them Torah, as it is said (Deuteronomy 11): ״ולמדתם אותם את בניכם,״ and it is written (Isaiah 48): ״אני ה׳ מלמדך להועיל.״ To teach him a trade — so the Holy One, blessed be He, taught them the commandments, as it is said (Leviticus 27): ״אלה המצות אשר צוה ה׳.״ To marry him to a wife — so the Holy One, blessed be He, said to them (Genesis 1): ״פרו ורבו.״ Just as a father feeds and gives drink, anoints, bathes, and clothes his son, so the Holy One, blessed be He, did for Israel, as it is said (Ezekiel 16:9–10): ״וארחצך במים ואשטוף דמיך מעליך ואסוכך בשמן ואלבישך רקמה״ etc., (ibid.): ״ולחמי אשר נתתי לך סלת ושמן ודבש האכלתיך,״ (Numbers 21): ״עלי באר ענו לה.״ Just as a father gives property to his son and his son is obligated to bring before him a gift, so the Holy One, blessed be He, said to Israel: ״כי תבאו אל ארץ מושבותיכם.״"], :book :numbers, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 15, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:32:42.951819220Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}